Six contemporary stained-glass windows designed by artist Claire Tabouret for Notre-Dame de Paris cathedral will be installed between October and November, then unveiled to the public in December, the public body overseeing the cathedral's restoration announced on Thursday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f49570c-873e-11f1-80df-81678484cde9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 10:04:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/6658e264-dc30-11f0-a7ba-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Photo-d-en-t%C3%AAte-3.jpg">© Baptiste Coulon/RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Wildfire sees 12,000 residents and tourists evacuated in south-west France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260723-wildfire-in-france-at-least-12-000-evacuated-in-the-south-west</link><description>
A wildfire near Bordeaux in south-west France has led to the evacuation of a further 7,000 people on Thursday, bringing the total number of tourists and residents moved to 12,000, local authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bfa146d8-8656-11f1-b1ad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2WK3WY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bfa146d8-8656-11f1-b1ad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2WK3WY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f0dd364e-8656-11f1-9660-85dd569f696a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 05:31:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/bfa146d8-8656-11f1-b1ad-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2WK3WY.jpg">AFP - ROMAIN PERROCHEAU</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French model recruiter with links to Epstein found dead near Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-french-model-recruiter-with-links-to-epstein-found-dead-near-paris</link><description>
French modelling scout Daniel Siad, 69, who had close ties to convicted American sex offender Jeffrey Epstein, has been found dead at his home outside Paris, prosecutors and his lawyer have said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ca242d4e-85b3-11f1-85b4-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-984A43L.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ca242d4e-85b3-11f1-85b4-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-984A43L.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">da8d5f8a-85d0-11f1-ab48-c7f48c98c05f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:44:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ca242d4e-85b3-11f1-85b4-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-984A43L.jpg">AFP - BRENDAN SMIALOWSKI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron talks environment minister out of quitting over pesticide U-turn</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-france-environment-minister-barbut-quits-then-stays-to-act-on-climate</link><description>
France's environment minister, Monique Barbut, will remain in her post, given the "urgency" to act on climate change, after submitting her resignation to President Emmanuel Macron over a bill to reintroduce bee-harming pesticides, her team said Wednesday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/32d28848-85ac-11f1-a609-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2Q32WF.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/32d28848-85ac-11f1-a609-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2Q32WF.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">93db5e38-85cc-11f1-9e26-739693c91962</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:18:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/32d28848-85ac-11f1-a609-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2Q32WF.jpg">AFP - THOMAS SAMSON</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fast-moving wildfire in southern France forces hundreds to flee</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-fast-moving-wildfire-in-southern-france-forces-hundreds-to-flee</link><description>
A fast-moving wildfire that broke out in the Var department in southern France has forced 400 people to flee their homes and burned more than 2,500 hectares – the latest in a string of fires amid three heatwaves since early June. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/80932f82-85ad-11f1-b485-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2TV7XU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/80932f82-85ad-11f1-b485-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2TV7XU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14b118fc-85b1-11f1-a2df-2d22df8298de</guid><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 11:50:53 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/80932f82-85ad-11f1-b485-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C2TV7XU.jpg">AFP - THIBAUD MORITZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French environment minister quits as new law opens door to contested pesticides</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260722-french-environment-minister-barbut-quits-as-farm-law-opens-door-to-contested-pesticides</link><description>
Environment Minister ⁠Monique Barbut has stepped ​down in protest after French lawmakers approved ​the controversial new agriculture bill allowing the temporary reintroduction of two pesticides accused of harming bees.
